      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Melt spinning of this alloy at rapid cooling rates can produce an amorphous structure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::005::1_introduction",
        "PMC11642357::web::020::4_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A roughly 5 nm Al2O3 layer can be deposited on mold or melt-container interfaces before melt spinning.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al2O3-coated processing route should use melt-spinning cooling rates above 10^6 K/s.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::005::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alloy should subsequently be reheated at 10–20 K/min through its DSC crystallization regime.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Processing under argon is suitable for this coated melt-spinning experiment.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11294451::web::032::bulk_sample_preparation"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The ultrathin Al2O3 coating will remain stable under the thermal conditions of rapid quenching.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al2O3 layer reduces heterogeneous nucleation sites at the molten-alloy interface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al2O3 layer acts as a chemical and physical barrier between the molten alloy and substrate impurities or oxide particulates.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing contact with substrate impurities or oxide particulates lowers the number of heterogeneous nucleation sites.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower heterogeneous nucleation-site density inhibits early formation of primary crystalline phases during rapid solidification.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower heterogeneous nucleation-site density delays crystallization during reheating.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Coated samples will retain a higher amorphous fraction than otherwise identical uncoated samples.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Coated samples will have a higher crystallization-onset temperature than uncoated samples.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slow or less rapid cooling of this alloy produces a complex multiphase crystalline microstructure, whereas faster cooling reduces crystallization and can yield an amorphous structure.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::005::1_introduction",
        "PMC11642357::web::019::4_discussion",
        "PMC11642357::web::020::4_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Uncoated processing gives an earlier crystallization onset during reheating than Al2O3-passivated processing.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant melt-spinning boundary is above 10^6 K/s.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::005::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant reheating window is 10–20 K/min up to approximately 600–650 °C.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is applicable to thin-plate or ribbon samples.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::005::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nucleation from impurities away from the mold interface and loss of coating uniformity under extreme thermal gradients may limit the intervention.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
